  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the key uncertainty is whether a multimodal fusion architecture with a learned RNA encoder can establish a strong performance baseline. Config_002 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, resnet50, transformer, weighted) tests this hypothesis by combining both modalities with a sophisticated RNA encoder (scgpt), a robust image encoder (resnet50, lower overfitting risk than ViT-L), transformer aggregation for profile-level information, and weighted fusion. This is the best first experiment because: (1) it establishes a high-performance reference point to guide ablation in subsequent experiments, (2) it uses multiprofile to maximize information from the profile modality, and (3) if it performs well, the remaining 9 experiments can systematically ablate each component (encoder choice, aggregation, fusion type, profile setting) to identify what drives accuracy; if it underperforms, it signals that a simpler or different architectural direction is needed. This balances exploration of the most promising architectural hypothesis with practical robustness."
}

